    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nPressing `=` to synchronize and then pressing `n` to discard changes breaks `mini.files` when `preview = true`. \r\nThis does not happen if `preview = false/nil`.\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNightly (19fb573)\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. `nvim -nu minimal.lua`\r\n2. Open the explorer: `lua MiniFiles.open()<cr>`\r\n3. Start editing entries (e.g. press `o`)\r\n4. Write something: `qwerty`\r\n5. Return to normal mode\r\n6. Press `=`\r\n7. Press `n`\r\n8. Observe an error\r\n\r\nNote: `preview = true`\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Minimal configuration</summary>\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal root = '/tmp/nvim'\r\n\r\nfor _, name in ipairs({ 'config', 'data', 'state', 'cache' }) do\r\n  vim.env[('XDG_%s_HOME'):format(name:upper())] = root .. '/' .. name\r\nend\r\n\r\nlocal lazy_path = root .. '/plugins/lazy.nvim'\r\nif not vim.loop.fs_stat(lazy_path) then\r\n  vim.api.nvim_cmd({\r\n    cmd = '!',\r\n    args = {\r\n      'git',\r\n      'clone',\r\n      '--filter=blob:none',\r\n      '--single-branch',\r\n      'https://github.com/folke/lazy.nvim.git',\r\n      lazy_path,\r\n    },\r\n  }, {})\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:prepend(lazy_path)\r\n\r\nlocal plugins = {\r\n  { 'folke/lazy.nvim' },\r\n  { 'AlexvZyl/nordic.nvim' },\r\n  -- plugins\r\n  { 'echasnovski/mini.files' },\r\n}\r\n\r\nrequire('lazy').setup(plugins, {\r\n  root = root .. '/plugins',\r\n})\r\nlocal mini_files = require('mini.files')\r\nmini_files.setup({\r\n  windows = {\r\n    preview = true,\r\n  },\r\n})\r\n\r\nvim.opt.termguicolors = true\r\nvim.cmd.colorscheme('nordic')\r\n\r\n```\r\n</details>\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nBeing able to use `mini.files` if I discard changes.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\nWhen trying to close `mini.files` or sync changes `neovim` prints this error:\r\n```\r\nE5108: Error executing lua: /tmp/nvim/plugins/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:2005: attempt to compare number with nil\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        /tmp/nvim/plugins/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:2005: in function 'is_modified_buffer'\r\n        /tmp/nvim/plugins/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:2158: in function 'window_update_border_hl'\r\n        /tmp/nvim/plugins/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:2151: in function 'window_set_view'\r\n        /tmp/nvim/plugins/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:1472: in function 'explorer_refresh_depth_window'\r\n        /tmp/nvim/plugins/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:1252: in function 'explorer_refresh'\r\n        /tmp/nvim/plugins/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:733: in function </tmp/nvim/plugins/mini.files/lua/mini/files.lua:725>\r\n```",
